      "evidence_points": "The CVE description states that \"accumulated size can wrap past 65535, causing the pointer arithmetic... to land within already-written ACEs,\" and the patch diff confirms the fix by replacing direct additions with `check_add_overflow()` calls (e.g., `if (check_add_overflow(*size, ace_sz, size)) break;`) in `fs/smb/server/smbacl.c`."
